  "verbalization": "Neogitogenin appears to have a complex relationship with ME-180 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Neogitogenin to CAKI-2, which is then targeted by Levopimaric acid, and finally, Levopimaric acid targets ME-180. The second pathway connects Neogitogenin to Sucrose porin, which in turn targets ME-180. The third pathway also links Neogitogenin to CAKI-2, which is targeted by Npc255577, and Npc255577 targets ME-180. These pathways suggest that Neogitogenin may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence ME-180, potentially through the modulation of various targets. The evidence supports a possible role for Neogitogenin in modulating pathways that ultimately affect ME-180, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Neogitogenin to interact with multiple targets, underscoring the complexity of its biological effects.",
